+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {"tags": ["hide"]},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import seaborn.objects as so\n",
+    "from seaborn import load_dataset\n",
+    "penguins = load_dataset(\"penguins\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "`Perc` replaces the observations in each group with one row for each requested percentile. By default, `k=5` produces the endpoints and quartiles (0, 25, 50, 75, and 100). The computed value is stored on the value axis, and the level is recorded in a `percentile` column. An integer `k` requests that many evenly spaced levels from 0 through 100; a list gives explicit levels."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc())"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Choose a different number of evenly spaced levels with an integer `k`:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc(k=3))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Pass a list to request specific levels. The `method` parameter selects NumPy's percentile method; it defaults to `linear`. NumPy's valid choices are `inverted_cdf`, `averaged_inverted_cdf`, `closest_observation`, `interpolated_inverted_cdf`, `hazen`, `weibull`, `linear`, `median_unbiased`, `normal_unbiased`, `lower`, `higher`, `midpoint`, and `nearest`."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc(k=[10, 50, 90], method=\"nearest\"))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Combining `Perc` with `Range` draws an interval between requested percentile values:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
